I fixed `peek()` and the tests pass: `node test.js` prints `OK`.

The bug was an off-by-one error in `stack.js:5`. `peek()` read `this.items[this.items.length]`, which is one position past the end of the array, so it always returned `undefined`. It now reads `this.items[this.items.length - 1]`, which is the item pushed most recently, and it doesn't remove anything. I also deleted the `// BUG` comment on that line.

On an empty stack, `peek()` returns `undefined`, while `pop()` throws `"empty"`. The tests don't check this case. If you want the two to behave the same way, I can make `peek()` throw too.


